---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
import { withBase } from '../utils';
---

<Layout
	title="About Me"
	description="Why I write chemical literature reviews"
	pubDate={new Date('15 Sept. 2026')}
>
	<p>
		I'm Benedict D. Ticehurst, and this site is where I publish my reviews of the chemical
		literature.
	</p>

	<p>
		I write them as part of my own ongoing research and study. Working through a topic properly
		means reading widely across the primary literature, and I've found that the only way to
		actually retain and use that reading is to write it up: pull the relevant papers together,
		work out where they agree and where they don't, and end up with a single account I can go back
		to later. Writing a review forces a level of rigor that just taking notes doesn't.
	</p>

	<p>
		Publishing them here rather than keeping them as private notes is partly accountability — a
		public write-up has to actually hold together — and partly because a well-referenced summary of
		a topic is useful to more people than just me. If you're working through the same literature,
		I'd rather you start from a synthesis than from scratch.
	</p>

	<p>
		These are reviews in the literature-review sense: a critical synthesis of published research on
		a topic, not a product rating or a recommendation. See the <a href={withBase('/blog')}>Reviews</a> for the
		current list.
	</p>
</Layout>
